{"name":"Mojo","hex":"#97463c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Mojo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Haramiyidae – certain mammals."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Moxo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mojo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mojo bag","blocks":[{"text":"A mojo bag, in the African American spiritual tradition called Hoodoo, is an amulet consisting of a flannel bag containing one or more magical items. It is a \"prayer in a bag\", or a spell that can be carried with or on the host's body. Alternative American names for the mojo bag include a toby, lucky hand, nation sack, conjure bag, and a package. Other forms of African American amulet bags include the gris-gris and juju bags."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mojo_bag","wikidata":"Q723903"},{"title":"Mojo (2017 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Mōjo is a 2017 Indian Kannada drama film written and directed by Sreesha Belakvaadi."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/cb/This_is_image_for_MOJO_kannada_film_released_recently.jpg/330px-This_is_image_for_MOJO_kannada_film_released_recently.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mojo_(2017_film)","wikidata":"Q48672797"},{"title":"Mojo (sauce)","blocks":[{"text":"Mojo is the name, or abbreviated name, of several types of sauces, varying in spiciness, consisting primarily of olive oil, local pepper varieties, garlic, paprika, cumin or coriander, and other spices. Mojo originated in the Canary Islands, where the main varieties are green mojo, red mojo, and spicy red mojo. Other countries have recipes similar to mojo, where acidic ingredients such as vinegar, lemon, orange, or lime juice may be used."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Papasarrugadas.jpg/330px-Papasarrugadas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mojo_(sauce)","wikidata":"Q2227032"},{"title":"Mojo (comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Mojo is a supervillain appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics, usually those featuring the X-Men family of characters. Created by writer Ann Nocenti and artist Arthur Adams, Mojo first appeared in Longshot #3, as the titular hero's archenemy, and subsequently a villain to the X-Men and their various sub-groups as well."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/05/Uncanny_X-Men_461.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mojo_(comics)","wikidata":"Q632369"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Grisgristuareg.JPG/500px-Grisgristuareg.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Grisgristuareg.JPG/500px-Grisgristuareg.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A West African Tuareg gris-gris","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrisgristuareg.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Minkisi_%28Kongo%2C_Landana%2C_Cabinda%29%2C_World_Museum_Liverpool.JPG/500px-Minkisi_%28Kongo%2C_Landana%2C_Cabinda%29%2C_World_Museum_Liverpool.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Minkisi_%28Kongo%2C_Landana%2C_Cabinda%29%2C_World_Museum_Liverpool.JPG/1280px-Minkisi_%28Kongo%2C_Landana%2C_Cabinda%29%2C_World_Museum_Liverpool.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Minkisi_%28Kongo%2C_Landana%2C_Cabinda%29%2C_World_Museum_Liverpool.JPG/500px-Minkisi_%28Kongo%2C_Landana%2C_Cabinda%29%2C_World_Museum_Liverpool.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Minkisi (Kongo - Central Africa), World Museum Liverpool - Minkisi cloth bundles were found on slave plantations in the United States in the Deep South. Minksi bundles influenced the creation of mojo bags in Hoodoo.[12][29]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMinkisi_(Kongo%2C_Landana%2C_Cabinda)%2C_World_Museum_Liverpool.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Mulatto_ex-slave_in_her_house_near_Greensboro%2C_Alabama%2C_May_..._%283109751881%29.jpg/500px-Mulatto_ex-slave_in_her_house_near_Greensboro%2C_Alabama%2C_May_..._%283109751881%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Mulatto_ex-slave_in_her_house_near_Greensboro%2C_Alabama%2C_May_..._%283109751881%29.jpg/500px-Mulatto_ex-slave_in_her_house_near_Greensboro%2C_Alabama%2C_May_..._%283109751881%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"African American women sewed charms and mojo hands into their quilts for spiritual protection. Newspaper is placed on the walls to ward off evil spirits.[58]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMulatto_ex-slave_in_her_house_near_Greensboro%2C_Alabama%2C_May_..._(3109751881).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e8/Grisgris.jpg/500px-Grisgris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e8/Grisgris.jpg/500px-Grisgris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gris-gris by Charles Gandolfo","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrisgris.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Zora_Neale_Hurston_and_unidentified_man_1935_Belle_Glade_FL.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Zora_Neale_Hurston_and_unidentified_man_1935_Belle_Glade_FL.tif.jpg?utm_sou